<h2>1. Where to send a complaint</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:founder@jannayaks.in">founder@jannayaks.in</a> with the subject line “Grievance / Profile Complaint”. Include your name and contact details, the profile URL or application reference, the nature of the complaint, the specific material in question and the action you want us to take.</p>
<p>For copyright, trademark, privacy or impersonation complaints, identify the right or interest affected and give enough information for us to assess the claim. Do not send passwords, OTPs or unnecessary sensitive personal data.</p>

<h2>2. Personal data requests and complaints</h2>
<p>You can use the same channel to ask for access to a summary of your personal data, to ask for correction, completion, updating or erasure, to withdraw consent, to nominate another person to exercise your rights if you die or become incapacitated, or to complain about how we have handled your personal data. Please write from your registered email address where possible so that we can verify the request.</p>

<h2>3. Complaints about a profile</h2>
<p>A complaint may concern inaccurate information, lack of consent, impersonation, privacy, defamation, intellectual-property infringement, unlawful material, a safety concern or a breach of our Terms. Where reasonably possible, we may contact the profile owner or applicant for a response. We may temporarily restrict access while assessing a credible and urgent complaint.</p>

<h2>4. Takedown and corrective action</h2>
<p>Depending on the nature and urgency of the complaint, action may include correction, adding context, disabling a link, restricting access, temporarily hiding a profile, removing material, suspending an account or rejecting an application. We may act on a valid court order, government direction or other legally binding notice. We may also take proportionate action where reasonably necessary to protect privacy, safety, rights, security or compliance with law.</p>
<p>We do not promise that every allegation will result in removal. We assess complaints on the information available, applicable law, urgency, the rights of affected persons and the need to prevent misuse of the complaint process.</p>

<h2>5. Acknowledgement and timelines</h2>
<p>We will acknowledge your complaint promptly and respond within the time limits prescribed by applicable law. For grievances about personal data, that means the period prescribed by the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025. Where another statutory rule applies to the complaint type, its timeline prevails. We will tell you the outcome and any further information we need.</p>

<h2>6. Grievance Officer and contact for privacy questions</h2>
<p><strong>Designated Grievance Officer:</strong> Grievance Officer, Aurex Network (Proprietor).</p>
<p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:founder@jannayaks.in">founder@jannayaks.in</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Postal address:</strong> Aurex Network, a sole proprietorship operating from 3-532A, Manchadi Jn, Moongode P.O., Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala 695573, India.</p>
<p>This is also the contact for questions about how we process your personal data.</p>

<h2>7. If you are not satisfied</h2>
<p>If you are not satisfied with our response to a personal data grievance, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India once its complaint mechanism is in operation. The law expects you to have used our grievance process first.</p>

<h2>8. False or abusive complaints</h2>
<p>We may decline to act on complaints that are clearly abusive, fraudulent, irrelevant or unsupported, while still considering any credible information about a legal or safety risk.</p>
